    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0151" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1165</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-01T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1918,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 27, 4 p.m. Information received by the Department does not confirm
                    the report of serious conditions in Irkutsk. The Department is awaiting more
                    definite information as to Ambassador Francis’s plans. You will be communicated with later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
